# Grid Master — backend environment variables
#
# Copy the ones you use into your host's dashboard (Vercel: Settings →
# Environment Variables. Netlify: Site settings → Environment variables).
# None of these are required for the website itself to work — without any of
# them the booking form still functions via the FormSubmit fallback.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Booking e-mail relay (optional) — see docs/booking-email-setup.md
# Configure exactly ONE of the providers below so bookings are e-mailed from
# your own mail account instead of relying on FormSubmit's activation step.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Resend (https://resend.com) — easiest free option
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Brevo (https://brevo.com)
# BREVO_API_KEY=

# SendGrid (https://sendgrid.com)
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=

# Web3Forms (https://web3forms.com)
# WEB3FORMS_KEY=

# Any webhook that accepts a JSON POST (e.g. a Google Apps Script, Zapier, n8n)
# MAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Shared by every provider above
# MAIL_TO=contactgridmaster@gmail.com
# MAIL_FROM=Grid Master Website <onboarding@resend.dev>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Customer bookings → Google Sheet logger (optional, independent of e-mail)
# See docs/customer-bookings-sheet-setup.md for the full click-by-click setup.
# Every booking is appended as a row to a Google Sheet you own — download it
# any time as a real .xlsx file (File → Download → Microsoft Excel).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Apps Script "Web app" URL from Step 5 of the setup guide.
# MUST end in /exec — a /dev URL is the private test URL and never works.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# The same secret you set as the SHARED_SECRET script property in Step 3.
# It must match EXACTLY (no quotes, no trailing space) or every booking is
# silently rejected by the script.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_SECRET=

# After changing either value you MUST redeploy — environment variables only
# reach a NEW deployment. Then check everything at:
#
#   /api/booking-health?selftest=1
#
# That endpoint is read-only, writes nothing to the sheet, never reveals the
# secret (only an 8-character fingerprint), and tells you in plain English
# which step is misconfigured.
